      "text": "Rotary Position Embedding (RoPE) is a positional encoding technique for transformers that represents token positions by rotating query and key vectors in a complex plane. Instead of adding fixed or learned position vectors, RoPE applies a rotation matrix parameterized by the token's absolute position, which causes the attention score between two tokens to depend only on their relative distance. This property allows models to generalize better to longer sequences and has become the default in major open-weight LLMs such as LLaMA, Mistral, and Gemma."
